# Copy this file to .env and fill in the one blank at the top.
#
# NOTE, if you arrived from `00_minimal`: there is deliberately no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here. In that
# example it is your real key and the agent is given it. Here the agent is given a fixed
# placeholder, set in `compose.yml` and worth nothing, and your real credential goes in
# MODEL_AUTH_VALUE below, which only the `model-proxy` service ever sees. Setting
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in this file has no effect.

# The model credential, and the MODEL PROXY's alone. Neither the Gateway nor the agent is given
# it: the proxy holds it and sets the header on the way out, so the agent authenticates to nothing
# and has nothing to leak. That is the whole difference between this example and `00_minimal`,
# where the agent holds the key in its own environment and can read it with `env`.
#
# It is the header VALUE, because providers spell it differently:
#
#   Anthropic (the default)          MODEL_AUTH_VALUE=sk-ant-...
#   OpenAI-compatible, e.g. OpenRouter
#     MODEL_AUTH_VALUE=Bearer sk-or-v1-...
#     MODEL_UPSTREAM_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api
#     MODEL_AUTH_HEADER=authorization
#     and on `agent`, OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://model-proxy:8080/v1 in place of ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL
MODEL_AUTH_VALUE=

# Where the proxy forwards to, and which header it sets.
# The proxy PRESERVES THE PATH: it appends whatever the agent asked for to this URL. So this must
# not repeat a segment the agent's own base URL already carries. Anthropic's SDK asks for
# `/v1/messages`, so this is the bare origin; an OpenAI-compatible base URL ending in `/v1` means
# this one ends before it (`.../api`, not `.../api/v1`), or the path comes out as `/v1/v1/...`.
MODEL_UPSTREAM_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
MODEL_AUTH_HEADER=x-api-key

# The seeded User's password, which `main.ts` sets from trusted code on the first boot and the
# `tui` service logs in with. Handing a Gateway its users' plaintext passwords through the
# environment is a demo affordance so that `docker compose up` is the whole setup. Nothing about
# it is worth copying: a real deployment sets a password out of band and never holds one here.
USER_PASSWORD=correct horse battery staple
